@*
    The reveal control for a password field. Wrap it and the input together in a
    <div class="password-field"> so the button can sit inside the input's box.

    Hidden entirely without the shell script, which is what performs the toggle:
    a button that did nothing would be worse than no button, because it looks
    like the field is refusing to reveal rather than like the feature is absent.

    The label is the accessible name and it changes with the state, so a screen
    reader announces what the button will do next rather than only that it is
    pressed. Both icons are rendered and CSS shows one, which keeps the swap off
    the main thread and free of a flash while an SVG is parsed.
*@
<button type="button"
        class="password-field__toggle"
        data-shell-password-toggle
        aria-pressed="false"
        aria-label="Show password"
        title="Show password">
    <span class="password-field__icon password-field__icon--show">
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_Icon", "eye")
    </span>
    <span class="password-field__icon password-field__icon--hide">
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_Icon", "eye-off")
    </span>
</button>
